  Rock Mountain -> home with SHA-256 identical at every hop (85b5071), a public gap
  analysis (4dc2e8d; 19 gaps, five majors), and the fix pass (a7d92d7; SQ daemon mode
  only, all five majors fixed, regressions 35/35). Will challenged the headline resume
  figure ("353 KB to 1 KB sounds like undetected failure") and he was right to: Emise's
  first re-tests were INVALID (measurements against a 0-byte store left by a failed
  teleport-in on the pre-fix binary — exactly the failure shape he named). The scripted
  detector suite then PROVED change detection (tests/change_detection.sh 7/7; root cause
  was an SQ daemon single-slot mailbox race in ocbox's writer, fixed with a readiness
  gate and proven-dead-only recovery); final scoreboard 94/94, published faa9f91.
