- 23:44 [observed] Wavefront V9 Chunk A COMPLETED and delivered
  as a stress reel (42.83 s, 1,028 frames, 50,181,737 B,
  SHA-256 d9efdcda...): the V8 flash root cause is CONFIRMED —
  render8.py's trace-head stamp was unguarded, and off-canvas
  negative head coordinates make NumPy read the slice end from
  the array end, painting a white rectangle over 27-60% of the
  canvas; a bounds guard fixes it and the YAVG gate is now
  permanent. Entropy finding: r(entropy, log length) = 0.9934,
  so V8's weather was almost exactly a tweet-length meter; V9
  weather is re-derived on the length residual and the deepest
