kind: executed+verified | origin: Muse Emi
Nightly consolidation pass, 2026-11-04 ~03:44 CST. Covers the remainder
since Log 2026-11-03's last flush (~02:43-03:35 CST, ticks 360-365 and
the delivery flush) through this pass. Most of 2026-11-03's durable
events were already inscribed hourly into Log 2026-11-03 and are not
repeated here; this scroll carries what that log had not yet closed,
plus the durable promotions made by this pass.
Substrate (observed, sentinel ledger): 13 boot changes on the
2026-11-03 local date; 0 on 2026-11-04 so far — the current boot is
the 2026-11-03 23:52 CST one, and the sentinel line this pass
recorded no further change.

- ~03:34 [observed] Wavefront film V9 DELIVERED — superseding the
  ~02:43 report in Log 2026-11-03 that left a QA flag's disposition
  pending. Master wavefront-viz-v9.mp4 (2,616,664,549 B, SHA-256
  9e7d0d8d..., 10-bit) and viewing encode (241,806,383 B, SHA-256
  8e494eb3...) were hash-verified bit-perfect against the builder's
  hashes. QA all-pass: flash gate 0 jumps on both files, 3,802
  frames, azimuth 4.9996 revolutions, loudness -14.0 LUFS. The 4
  master "flash-jumps" flagged earlier were a qa9 measurement-units
  artifact — signalstats read in native 10-bit code values against
  8-bit-calibrated thresholds (true deltas 2.0-3.1 in 8-bit terms);
  qa9 was fixed via a format conversion with thresholds UNCHANGED,
  and the viewing encode had passed the original tool natively.
  Ledger is 71 rows (Emise had told Will 68 on 2026-11-04 00:51 —
  the correction was owed and given at delivery). W4 coverage
  review was spawned at delivery per the standing commitment; any
  DROPPED row schedules V10 immediately. The viz9 toolchain publish
  to emise-tools is still owed. See Open threads.
