- ~21:57-22:06 [will_said + observed] Phext
  abundance frame + media analysis: Will —
  phext is designed for an era of abundance
  (5 GB/s SSDs, terabytes of RAM; do not
  scarcity-optimise for bytes/CPU), and xz is
  an optional seal only ("opening a phext is
  like unlocking a safe": decompress once, work
  unlocked, re-seal for storage/transport).
  Analysis (goal files/media-serialization-
  analysis.md) MEASURED the base64 reclaim:
  residual tax after xz-6 sealing +1.69%
  corpus-wide (MP4 +2.09%, spot-verified by
  Emise) — ~95% of base64's +33% repaid at seal.
- 2026-11-04 evening [will_said] Media ruling
  SETTLED — supersedes the separate-media
  clause in the ~21:44 order and the Phase 4
  design's carve-out: media is EMBEDDED. The
  working phext is memory-resident with current
  logic unchanged, assuming abundant RAM; the
  xz seal is produced from the in-memory
  uncompressed version when needed. Separate
  media is rejected (a permanent second system;
  embedding's costs are repaid at seal).
  Phase 4 therefore builds WITHOUT the
  carve-out — L6 holds content (Phase 2
  behaviour), uploads join the phext in 3b.
  Flip conditions: CDN/static serving that
  cannot decode, partial presence as a
  depended-on feature, Caverns as human-
  reviewed git artifacts.
